            {
              "id": "05b8abbc-7172-3f48-8379-59ad0dbfb7f3",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "This finding is classified as a genuine vulnerability because the analysis identified a risk of undefined behavior due to possible overlap between the source and destination memory regions in the memory copy operation. The destination and source expressions are related by data flow, which means that the memory areas may overlap, leading to undefined behavior according to the C standard for memory copy functions. Additionally, there is no explicit check to ensure that the source is not null, which further increases the risk. The destination is not likely to be null, but the overlap and potential null source pointer make this a high-confidence issue that should be addressed. The classification and verdict both indicate a genuine problem.\n\n## In Context Remediation\nTo prevent undefined behavior when copying memory, ensure that the source and destination memory regions do not overlap. If there is any possibility of overlap, use `memmove` instead of `memcpy`, as `memmove` is designed to handle overlapping regions safely. Additionally, add explicit checks to ensure that the source pointer is not null before performing the copy operation.\n\n```cpp\nif (nopData != nullptr) {\n    memmove(buf + sizeof(addrInst) + sizeof(stdBr), nopData, sizeof(nopData));\n}\n```\n\nThis change replaces `memcpy` with `memmove` and adds a null check for the source pointer, mitigating both the undefined behavior from overlapping regions and the risk of dereferencing a null pointer.\n\n## References\n- [OWASP C-Based Toolchain Hardening Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/C-Based_Toolchain_Hardening_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-119: Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/119.html)\n- [CWE-120: Buffer Copy without Checking Size of Input ('Classic Buffer Overflow')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/120.html)\n- [CWE-787: Out-of-bounds Write](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/787.html)\n- [OWASP Buffer Overflow](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/Buffer_Overflow)\n\n___\n"
