            {
              "id": "94f46ffa-57eb-3f1f-9d38-2f223c5be768",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "This finding is considered a genuine vulnerability because the destination buffer's capacity is not known or proven to be sufficient for the number of bytes being copied. The code copies 4 bytes from a string literal into a buffer, but there is no information about the size of the destination buffer. This means there is a risk of writing past the end of the buffer if it is smaller than 4 bytes, which can lead to memory corruption or security vulnerabilities. The use of a string literal as the source reduces the risk of certain issues (such as undefined behavior from overlapping memory), but does not mitigate the risk of a buffer overflow. There are no explicit checks or guards to ensure the destination buffer is large enough, and the count is a fixed literal rather than being derived from the buffer's actual size. The classification and verdict both indicate a high-confidence, actionable issue.\n\n## In Context Remediation\nBefore copying data into the buffer, ensure that the destination buffer is at least as large as the number of bytes being copied. If the buffer size is not known, add a check or use a safer approach. For example, if you know the buffer's size in advance, compare it to the number of bytes to be copied:\n\n```cpp\nsize_t buf_size = /* actual size of buf */;\nif (buf_size >= 4) {\n    memcpy(buf, \"\\177ELF\", 4);\n} else {\n    // Handle error: buffer too small\n}\n```\nIf the buffer size is not available, consider redesigning the code to pass the buffer size along with the buffer pointer, or use a safer function that takes the buffer size as an argument.\n\n## References\n- [OWASP C-Based Toolchain Hardening Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/C-Based_Toolchain_Hardening_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [OWASP Buffer Overflow](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/Buffer_Overflow)\n- [CWE-119: Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/119.html)\n- [CWE-120: Buffer Copy without Checking Size of Input ('Classic Buffer Overflow')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/120.html)\n- [CWE-787: Out-of-bounds Write](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/787.html)\n\n___\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "DS121708"
