            {
              "id": "26747b73-aa5d-3cca-9086-a82f587d0fd5",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "This finding is classified as a genuine vulnerability because the analysis identified a risk of undefined behavior due to possible overlap between the source and destination memory regions in the memory copy operation. The verdict is supported by the classification indicating undefined behavior risk and the explicit 'GENUINE' verdict. The analysis determined that overlap is feasible based on data flow between the destination and source, which can cause unpredictable results with functions like memcpy. Additionally, there is a risk that the source pointer may be null at this location, as there is no prior check ensuring it is non-null. The destination is not likely to be null, reducing risk in that direction. No explicit buffer size or guard is present to ensure safe copying, and the destination is a pointer without a known capacity, increasing the risk of memory safety issues. These factors together confirm the presence of a real vulnerability.\n\n## In Context Remediation\nTo prevent undefined behavior when copying memory where the source and destination regions may overlap, use `memmove` instead of `memcpy`. `memmove` is designed to handle overlapping memory regions safely. Replace the original call with:\n\n```cpp\nmemmove(buf, tailMergeX64, sizeof(tailMergeX64));\n```\n\nAdditionally, ensure that both the source and destination pointers are valid and not null before performing the copy. For example:\n\n```cpp\nif (buf != nullptr && tailMergeX64 != nullptr) {\n    memmove(buf, tailMergeX64, sizeof(tailMergeX64));\n}\n```\n\nThis change eliminates the risk of undefined behavior due to overlapping memory regions and null pointer dereference.\n\n## References\n- [CWE-119: Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/119.html)\n- [CWE-787: Out-of-bounds Write](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/787.html)\n- [OWASP: Buffer Overflow](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/Buffer_Overflow)\n- [OWASP C-Based Toolchain Hardening Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/C-Based_Toolchain_Hardening_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n\n___\n"
              },
              "properties": {
